  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>named_entity_recognition - finds the entities in ten business documents two ways, with Stanford CoreNLP
and with a local LLM, and writes both lists side by side.
Needs the GenAI plugins with a GENAI-EE license, PDI started with -Xmx4g (PENTAHO_DI_JAVA_OPTIONS)
for CoreNLP, and Ollama at OLLAMA_URL with MODEL_NAME pulled.

1. csvi-documents: CSV file input, ../ner_documents.csv: document_id, source, text. Copies its rows to both
   branches.
2. ner-corenlp: NER Extractor, Stream, Binary Datum field text, annotators tokenize,ssplit,pos,lemma,ner,
   result ner_json (JSON array with offsets).
3. json-ner: JSON input from ner_json: entity_text $[*].text, entity_type $[*].ner (one row per entity).
4. const-method-ner: Add constants, method = NER Extractor.
5. sv-ner: keeps document_id, source, method, entity_text, entity_type.
6. const-instruction: Add constants, run_instruction (ten custom entity types and the JSON shape), method
   = AI Chat.
7. ai-extract: AI Chat x${STEP_COPIES}, Stream message text, run instruction run_instruction, Ollama
   ${MODEL_NAME} at ${OLLAMA_URL}, temperature 0, numCtx 4096, timeout 180, result llm_json.
8. json-llm: JSON input from llm_json: entity_text $.entities[*].text, entity_type $.entities[*].type.
9. sv-llm: the same five fields as sv-ner.
10. sort-entities: Sort rows by document_id, method, entity_type; copies its rows to txt-entities and
    grp-counts.
11. txt-entities: entities.csv beside this file, one row per entity per method.
12. grp-counts / txt-counts: Group by document_id, method, entity_count = number of rows (COUNT_ALL
    of entity_text); entity_counts.csv.

Shipped data: 10 documents of 10 kinds, from a customer email to an HR memo.</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>623</width>
      <heigth>458</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>167</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>224</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>245</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
